  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Solve \\(x^2-4x-1=0\\) by completing the square. Which option gives the correct completed-square equation and result?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((x-2)^2=3\\), \\(x=2\\pm\\sqrt{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\((x+2)^2=5\\), \\(x=-2\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\)",
    "C": "\\((x-2)^2=5\\), \\(x=2\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\)",
    "D": "\\((x-4)^2=17\\), \\(x=4\\pm\\sqrt{17}\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Rearranging gives \\(x^2-4x=1\\). Adding \\((4/2)^2=4\\) to both sides gives \\((x-2)^2=5\\), so \\(x=2\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\). A's right-hand side is incorrect because adding \\(4\\) to \\(1\\) gives \\(5\\), not \\(3\\). B has a sign error, and D adds the wrong number when completing the square. The correct choice is C.",
